# 3-Tier AI Fallback Architecture

This plan covers the enterprise integration of a massive 3-platform cascading AI failure-avoidance engine parsing physical supplier PDFs.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Persistent Counter & Limits ([lib/aiParser.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts))
* Initialize a global memory object surviving Node process cycles (because the App runs persistently on Debian):
  ```typescript
  let dailyUsage = { date: new Date().toDateString(), gemini: 0, groq: 0 };
  ```
* Intercept PDF requests to `checkAndResetDailyUsage()` at midnight.
* Skip Tier 1 (Gemini) completely if `dailyUsage.gemini >= 1400`.
* Skip Tier 2 (Groq) completely if `dailyUsage.groq >= 14000`.

### 2. The 3-Tier Parsing Chain ([lib/aiParser.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts))
* **TIER 1 (Google Gemini Primary):**
  * Map to `generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/gemini-2.0-flash:generateContent`.
  * Convert incoming PDF stream to raw `base64` and inject directly into the visual parsing array.
  * If hit succeeds: return `result`, add `provider: 'gemini'`, increment `gemini` counter.
  * If `HTTP 429` Rate Limit caught: auto-execute Tier 2 sequence.
* **TIER 2 (Groq Primary Fallback):**
  * Use the existing server-side text extraction (or `pdf-parse` if installed) bounding extraction limits up to 100 pages.
  * Map the string to `api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions` using native `llama-3.3-70b-versatile`.
  * If hit succeeds: return `result`, add `provider: 'groq'`, increment `groq` counter.
  * If `HTTP 429` Rate Limit caught: auto-execute Tier 3 sequence.
* **TIER 3 (OpenRouter Slow-Mode Final Guard):**
  * Modify existing string chunker looping mechanism inside [parseChunkWithAI](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#349-389).
  * Break loop via explicitly injecting `await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 15000))` (15 seconds) inside iterating slices.
  * Emits `provider: 'openrouter'`.

### 3. DOM & Output Headers (`app/api/medicines/parse-pdf/route.ts` & Frontend UI)
* Expose `X-AI-Provider` headers actively streaming from API backend.
* Inject `Processed by Google Gemini ✓`, `Processed by Groq ✓`, or `Processed by OpenRouter (slow mode) ✓` dynamically into the generic Import Success UI DOM response logic.

## Verification Plan
### Functional Flow Hooks
- Simulate specific `HTTP 429` cascade boundaries mocking Node native [fetch](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/settings/user-settings.tsx#74-100) intercepts to verify Fallback traversal paths.
- Evaluate standard output mappings inside exact component state trees.
